<h1>lhohq</h1>
<span class="sub">the house of hollow houses</span>
<span class="glyph l">♂ &nbsp; ✺ &nbsp; ❆</span>
<p class="cormorant center">you have arrived at a place that was not waiting for you.</p>
<hr>
<p>Do not stand at the centre of the <a href="/landing/">landing</a>. The centre of the <a href="/landing/">landing</a> is, by long arrangement, reserved for the <a href="/turret/">turret</a>, which is not, at the time of writing, in the building.</p><p>The <a href="/buttery/">buttery</a> keeps the keys <span class="flicker">to</span> the <a href="/apse/">apse</a>. The <a href="/apse/">apse</a> keeps the keys to the <a href="/columbarium/">columbarium</a>. The <a href="/columbarium/">columbarium</a> keeps no keys; the <a href="/columbarium/">columbarium</a> is, the house insists, beyond locking.</p><svg class="eye" width="220" height="120" viewBox="0 0 220 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <g fill="none" stroke="#2a2a2a" stroke-width="1">
      <path d="M5,60 Q110,5 215,60 Q110,115 5,60 Z"/>
      <ellipse cx="110" cy="60" rx="94" ry="17"/>
      <circle cx="110" cy="60" r="24"/>
      <circle cx="110" cy="60" r="12" fill="#2a2a2a" />
    </g></svg><h2>i. on entering</h2><p class="type">Of all the rooms in the house, the <a href="/dressing/">dressing</a> is the one the house is least proud of. The house has been asked, on <span class="tilt-l">more</span> than one occasion, to demolish it. The house has, on more than one occasion, declined.</p><p class="indent">There is a <a href="/oubliette/">oubliette</a> on the floor. There is, properly speaking, a <a href="/oubliette/">oubliette</a> for every floor. The house has confirmed this; the house keeps <span class="faint">records;</span> the records are kept in the <a href="/alcove/">alcove</a>, which is, in turn, on a floor of its own.</p><p class="huge tilt-3 smear">up &nbsp; <span class="flicker">up</span></p><p>Three visitors entered the <a href="/hall/">hall</a> on the same morning, in 1971. Only two of them, when the count was taken, could be accounted for. The third is, the house assures us, in the <a href="/scullery/">scullery</a>, and is well, and prefers not to be disturbed.</p><p class="tilt-r">The lock on the door of the <a href="/oratory/">oratory</a> is on the inside. The key is in the <a href="/henhouse/">henhouse</a>. Visitors are <span class="faint">advised</span> to plan accordingly.</p><p>It is not advisable to read aloud in the <a href="/chantry/">chantry</a>. The <a href="/chantry/">chantry</a> retains what it hears, and it has, over <span class="shake">the</span> years, learned to recite.</p><p>Do not stand at the centre of the <a href="/stable/">stable</a>. The centre of the <a href="/stable/">stable</a> is, <span class="tilt-l">by</span> long arrangement, reserved for the <a href="/ballroom/">ballroom</a>, which is not, at the time of writing, in the building.</p><h2>ii. on the obedient</h2><p>The obedient have always been answered first, and the answer issued to them is a catalogue, organised alphabetically, of every place the <a href="/atrium/">atrium</a> is not. The catalogue is, by long custom, kept at the front gate, in a small text file the house permits to be read by anyone who knows to ask for it. <em>It is, of course, a complete list.</em></p><p class="smear">The <a href="/mill/">mill</a> keeps the keys <span class="tilt-l">to</span> the <a href="/music/">music</a>. The <a href="/music/">music</a> keeps the keys to the <a href="/crypt/">crypt</a>. The <a href="/crypt/">crypt</a> keeps no keys; the <a href="/crypt/">crypt</a> is, the house insists, beyond locking.</p><p class="cormorant">On the wall of the <a href="/scriptorium/">scriptorium</a> hangs <span class="tilt-l">a</span> portrait of the <a href="/buttery/">buttery</a>. The portrait is unsigned. The <a href="/buttery/">buttery</a> does not, on any account, recognise the likeness.</p><p class="fell">The <a href="/scullery/">scullery</a> keeps a list. The list is of every visitor who has ever asked, on entering, where the <a href="/nook/">nook</a> is. The list is bound; the list is long; the list is the <a href="/scullery/">scullery</a>, written down.</p><p>The <a href="/columbarium/">columbarium</a> was decorated, in 1903, by a woman who is now in the <a href="/nave/">nave</a>. She has not, on any subsequent occasion, asked to be moved.</p><p>The <a href="/stair/">stair</a> has been described, by certain visitors, as oppressive. The <a href="/alcove/">alcove</a> has, in writing, disagreed. <span class="tilt-l">The</span> matter is considered closed.</p>
<hr>
<h3>passages</h3><p class="cols tight tiny">the <a href="/study/">study</a>, the <a href="/alcove/">alcove</a>, the <a href="/oratory/">oratory</a>, the <a href="/library/">library</a>, the <a href="/drawing/"><span class="tilt-l">drawing</span></a>, the <a href="/scriptorium/">scriptorium</a>, the <a href="/granary/">granary</a>, the <a href="/chapel/">chapel</a>, the <a href="/watchtower/">watchtower</a>, the <a href="/refectory/">refectory</a>, the <a href="/lazaret/">lazaret</a>, the <a href="/attic/">attic</a>, the <a href="/atelier/">atelier</a>, the <a href="/lodge/">lodge</a>, the <a href="/vault/">vault</a>, the <a href="/cell/">cell</a>, the <a href="/cellar/"><em>cellar</em></a>, the <a href="/observatory/">observatory</a>, the <a href="/transept/"><span class="faint">transept</span></a>, the <a href="/ambulatory/"><span class="tilt-l">ambulatory</span></a>, the <a href="/gatehouse/">gatehouse</a>, the <a href="/columbarium/"><em>columbarium</em></a>, the <a href="/bathroom/">bathroom</a>, the <a href="/sacristy/">sacristy</a>, the <a href="/parlor/">parlor</a>, the <a href="/steeple/">steeple</a>, the <a href="/dressing/">dressing</a>, the <a href="/gallery/">gallery</a>, the <a href="/corridor/"><em>corridor</em></a>, the <a href="/mill/">mill</a>, the <a href="/mews/"><span class="faint">mews</span></a>, the <a href="/chantry/"><em>chantry</em></a>, the <a href="/dining/">dining</a>, the <a href="/scullery/"><em>scullery</em></a>, the <a href="/threshold/">threshold</a>, the <a href="/apse/">apse</a>, the <a href="/baptistery/">baptistery</a>, the <a href="/stable/">stable</a>, the <a href="/sitting/">sitting</a>, the <a href="/fascia/">fascia</a>.</p>
<p class="warn center breathe" style="opacity:.7;">the house thanks you for your visit. the house has already forgotten you.</p>
<p class="tiny faint center">est. <span class="reflected">MCMXLIV</span> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; visitor no. 8 4 4 1 3 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; the caretaker is elsewhere</p>

